From b8843b3b982b92acd991d5ac0a7d3f14818460bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:51:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Show client invoice payment status on category, bank and cash
 payroll screens

Payment priority decides whose salaries go first; this shows which clients
actually pay their invoices, and when, so default categories (Category A is
pre-ticked every month) can be judged on payment behaviour.

App\Support\ClientInvoiceStatus is the single rule, read by every screen:
- Month status: Paid (within 7 days of due date), Paid late, Part paid,
  Unpaid (not due yet), Overdue, No invoice. Uses invoices.status/due_date
  and receipts.receipt_month (payment date). Several invoices in a month are
  combined. One query per page.
- Payment record over the last 6 months: Pays on time / Pays late / Owing /
  No invoices. Invoices not yet due never count against a client.

Category page (categoryClients)
- "Invoice payments" column: record badge + one square per month with dates
  on hover. "Payment record" filter, also honoured by "Tick all matching".
- Default Category A card: lists defaults that are owing or pay late, with a
  button to untick the ones that owe before applying.
- Client panel: invoice history for 12 months (amount, due, paid on, owed).
- Fix: clicking a client name threw "MONTH_LABEL is not defined" (the panel
  script could not see the page script's constants), so the panel never
  loaded.

Bank / cash month pages
- CLIENT INVOICE column (status, when paid / days overdue, record) and chips
  that filter the table by client invoice status, alongside pay priority.
- Eager-load the relations the table prints: bank page 368 -> 13 queries.

Bank Excel export
- Columns P-R: client invoice status, paid/due detail, payment record
  (NET stays in N, PAY PRIORITY in O). "Client not paid" subtotal in Q4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
